-- Plainer 'what to do' wording for items whose detail was only a status line. Every sentence restates the Framework
-- (3.1, 1.3, 5.1) from sources already read in full (Building Act ss 105 and 108; Māori Reservations Regulations regs 4, 6, 15, 17, 19;
-- Charities Act ss 40 and 41). Guarded: only items that do not yet have 'What to do:' are changed. Safe to run more than once.
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if a building has a compliance schedule. That is any building other than a single home that has a specified system: sprinklers, a fire alarm or other emergency warning system, emergency lighting, or a lift (hand-held extinguishers do not count). What to do: 1) Ask the council whether each building has a compliance schedule. 2) If it does, give the council the Building Warrant of Fitness every year on the anniversary of the schedule, with the certificates from the independent qualified person who inspected the systems. 3) Display a copy where people using the building can easily see it, and keep the compliance schedule available. Not doing this is an offence: up to $50,000 for an individual, up to $150,000 for a body corporate. Sources: Building Act 2004, ss 105 and 108; building.govt.nz.' where name = 'Building Warrant of Fitness' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae land is a Māori reservation. All reservation money must go into a separate bank account that needs at least two authorised signatories (Māori Reservations Regulations 1994, reg 15). What to do: confirm the account is separate from other marae money and has two or more authorised signatories, and keep the bank''s confirmation with the trustee records. The Māori Land Court can ask to see the records, books and vouchers.' where name = 'Reservation money in a separate bank account with at least two authorised signatories' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae land is a Māori reservation. The trustees must hold an annual meeting each year, with at least 21 days'' notice, open to the beneficiaries (Māori Reservations Regulations 1994, reg 19). It may be held in person, online or both. What to do: send the notice at least 21 days ahead, invite the beneficiaries, and at the meeting outline the reservation''s position and work over the past 12 months and the proposals for the next 12. Keep the notice and the minutes as evidence.' where name = 'Annual meeting held with at least 21 days'' notice, open to beneficiaries' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae land is a Māori reservation. Trustees must publish notice of their appointment in a local newspaper within 7 days, and give any other notice the Māori Land Court directs (Māori Reservations Regulations 1994, reg 4). What to do: for each new trustee, place the notice within 7 days of the appointment, and keep a copy of the notice and the date it appeared.' where name = 'Notice of each trustee appointment published in a local newspaper within 7 days' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae land is a Māori reservation. Trustees must act in good faith, run the reservation so that it serves its purposes and benefits those entitled to use it, and follow the Act, the regulations and any court orders (Māori Reservations Regulations 1994, reg 6). What to do: make sure every trustee has read this. Good practice: record in the minutes when a new trustee has been told.' where name = 'Trustees know their duty to act in good faith and run the reservation for its purposes' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae land is a Māori reservation. Trustees must keep accurate, separate, up-to-date records of how the reservation is run, and produce them to the Māori Land Court if it asks (Māori Reservations Regulations 1994, reg 15). What to do: keep the reservation''s records apart from other marae business and keep them up to date. The Court can ask for the records, books and vouchers.' where name = 'Accurate, separate, up-to-date records of the reservation''s administration kept' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae land is a Māori reservation whose trustees are not a body corporate (if a body corporate is the trustee, regulation 16 applies instead). The first trustee meeting must be held within 30 days of appointment (Māori Reservations Regulations 1994, reg 17). The trustees appoint a chairperson, decide by majority (the chairperson has a casting vote) and record their proceedings in a minute book. What to do: hold the first meeting within 30 days, choose a chairperson, and start the minute book.' where name = 'First trustee meeting within 30 days of appointment; minute book kept' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae is a registered charity. File an annual return and a performance report (or the combined form for small charities) with Charities Services within 6 months of the balance date (Charities Act 2005, s 41). What to do: find the balance date, set the filing date as this item''s due date, file, and keep a copy. If a return is not filed or is incomplete, the charity cannot be found on the Charities Register, and repeated incomplete returns can lead to deregistration.' where name = 'Charities annual return and performance report filed within 6 months of balance date' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
update public.compliance_items set legal_basis_detail = 'Applies only if the marae is a registered charity. Tell Charities Services about any change to the name, address for service, balance date, rules, purposes or officers no later than three months after the change, or after the charity becomes aware of it (Charities Act 2005, s 40). This also covers a change that disqualifies an officer. What to do: when any of these change, notify Charities Services within three months and keep a copy of what was sent.' where name = 'Changes notified to Charities Services within 3 months (name, address, balance date, rules, purposes, officers)' and coalesce(legal_basis_detail,'') not like '%What to do:%';
